      "side": 1,
      "message": "can you just call pd_send_vdm()? or I guess, since that function also wakes the task, which we don\u0027t want to do here, you can create a new inline function to copy VDO data to buffer and call it as part of pd_send_vdm():\n\n/* Copy data into VDO output buffer and set VDO ready. The VDM state machine will automatically send in PD task */\nstatic inline void pd_queue_vdm(int port, uint32_t *data, int len)\n{\n  pd[port].vdm_state \u003d VDM_STATE_READY;\n  pd[port].vdo_count \u003d len;\n  memcpy(pd[port].vdo_data, data, sizeof(uint32_t) * len);\n}",
