      "side": 1,
      "message": "Now that we aren\u0027t sending VDM responses immediately in handle_requet(), we should be able to change this condition so that PDOs have higher priority:\n\n/* Do not send any PDOs if waiting for VDM response */\nif (pd[port].vdm_state \u003d\u003d VDM_STATE_BUSY)\n\nA couple things though. we need to change this in SRC_READY also. and we probably need to add code to the VDM state machine not to send a new VDO unless state is SRC_READY or SNK_READY, because if we give priority to PDOs, then we could transition to a DR_SWAP, PR_SWAP, or REQUEST state here, and we wouldn\u0027t want to send a VDO immediately after sending a power request. Basically, if a VDO is pending we shouldn\u0027t send a PDO, and if a PDO is pending we shouldn\u0027t send a VDO, and PDOs should have higher priority.",
